      "id": "claim_20f7ff5a69cd43e8aa9ad2bbc0f4f2ee",
      "statement": "deploy/regional/tests/claude_default_model.tftest.hcl verifies the claude_default_model <-> bedrock_model_agreements consistency guard in variables.tf: claude_default_model must be a known Bedrock inference-profile ID (a key in local.claude_inference_profile_foundation_models) that resolves to a foundation model present in bedrock_model_agreements, and bare foundation-model IDs are rejected even if that foundation model is itself approved. The suite uses mock_provider \"aws\" plus override_data for aws_partition and per-subnet AZ/VPC/route-table data to satisfy the module's Bedrock-endpoint and subnet_outbound_routing preconditions, so each plan run fails or succeeds only on the claude_default_model validation under test. Re-reading lines 93-136 confirms the run blocks (default_sonnet55_profile_succeeds, haiku55_requires_matching_agreement, approved_sonnet55_us_profile_succeeds, approved_sonnet55_eu_profile_succeeds) exercise exactly this validation with no other AWS behavior asserted.",
